  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Alstoyunine H and the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, as it is indirectly linked through multiple target pathways. Alstoyunine H is identified as a target of Caspase-5, which in turn is a target of two different compounds: WS-5995 B and Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate, both of which target the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. Similarly, 5-Oxobrucine, another compound targeting Caspase-5, also leads to the same subunit. These findings indicate that Alstoyunine H may exert its effects through Caspase-5, which is a key player in the proteasome pathway, suggesting a possible role in regulating proteasome function. The evidence is consistent across different compounds, but the strength of the relationship is moderate, as the scores are relatively similar across the paths. The mechanism appears to involve Caspase-5 as a central mediator, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction between Alstoyunine H and the proteasome subunit."
